# Real native processes, paired runner and owner session history require the phone/Mac.
[phone] Discover a spare native Claude conversation alongside the existing Codex sessions; verify visible history without private tool or thinking payloads.
[phone] Close the spare native process, send a harmless phone prompt, and verify a reply in the original session UUID with retained context and no duplicates after two scans.
[phone] Hold a spare conversation open and idle on the Mac, send a harmless phone prompt, and verify a new UUID on the same Soma thread with full prior context. Verify the original transcript is byte-for-byte unchanged.
[phone] Verify the copy note explains that the Mac window will not show phone messages. Send a second phone prompt and verify it continues the new UUID without another fork.
[phone] Hold a spare conversation busy on the Mac, send a harmless phone prompt, and verify a waiting note and no second model process. Let the Mac become idle; verify one forked reply on the same Soma thread.
[phone] Repeat the busy wait and cancel from Soma. Verify no phone model process starts and the native Mac process continues untouched.
[phone] Restart the idle runner; verify the phone copy and original alias do not appear as duplicate sessions, with no repeated history after two scans.
[phone] Verify unreadable or unverified holder metadata returns an explanatory refusal without queueing or starting a model.
